\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8.1}{\ignorespaces The Gordon growth model for a market paying a \$3 dividend next year, with dividends growing 4\% a year. Lowering the required return from 7\% to 6\% raises the price from \$100 to \$150 and lowers the dividend yield from 3\% to 2\%. High prices and low yields go with low expected returns.}}{123}{figure.caption.43}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:07-gordon}{{8.1}{123}{The Gordon growth model for a market paying a \$3 dividend next year, with dividends growing 4\% a year. Lowering the required return from 7\% to 6\% raises the price from \$100 to \$150 and lowers the dividend yield from 3\% to 2\%. High prices and low yields go with low expected returns}{figure.caption.43}{}}
